.Dd September 16, 2026
.Dt NDI_DC_ALLOCHDL 9F
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm ndi_dc_allochdl ,
.Nm ndi_dc_freehdl ,
.Nm ndi_dc_getname ,
.Nm ndi_dc_getaddr ,
.Nm ndi_dc_get_ap_data
.Nd copy in and access a device-control request
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/sunndi.h
.Ft "int"
.Fo ndi_dc_allochdl
.Fa "void *iocarg"
.Fa "struct devctl_iocdata **rdcp"
.Fc
.Ft "void"
.Fo ndi_dc_freehdl
.Fa "struct devctl_iocdata *dcp"
.Fc
.Ft "char *"
.Fo ndi_dc_getname
.Fa "struct devctl_iocdata *dcp"
.Fc
.Ft "char *"
.Fo ndi_dc_getaddr
.Fa "struct devctl_iocdata *dcp"
.Fc
.Ft "nvlist_t *"
.Fo ndi_dc_get_ap_data
.Fa "struct devctl_iocdata *dcp"
.Fc
.Sh INTERFACE LEVEL
illumos specific
.Pq Consolidation Private .
.Sh PARAMETERS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Va iocarg
User address of a \fBdevctl_iocdata\fP request.
.It Va rdcp
Address of a kernel pointer receiving the allocated request.
.It Va dcp
Valid request returned by \fBndi_dc_allochdl()\fP.
.El
.Sh DESCRIPTION
\fBndi_dc_allochdl()\fP copies a device-control request from the current user
process and returns an allocated kernel representation in \fB*rdcp\fP.
It converts the caller's data model, copies the node-name and unit-address
strings, and copies and unpacks an optional nvlist.
The request and referenced data must be user addresses; this is not an
\fBFKIOCTL\fP kernel-buffer copy interface.
.Pp
\fBndi_dc_getname()\fP and \fBndi_dc_getaddr()\fP return the copied child node name
and unit address.
\fBndi_dc_get_ap_data()\fP returns the unpacked nvlist supplied with the request.
An omitted field is returned as \fBNULL\fP.
The returned pointers belong to the handle and must not be freed separately.
.Pp
\fBndi_dc_freehdl()\fP frees the handle, its strings, and its nvlist.
Call it exactly once after a successful allocation when the request has been
processed.
Do not use the handle or any pointer obtained from it afterwards.
.Sh CONTEXT
\fBndi_dc_allochdl()\fP must be called from user context and may sleep.
The accessors and free function may be called from user or kernel context.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
\fBndi_dc_allochdl()\fP returns \fBNDI_SUCCESS\fP on success, \fBNDI_FAULT\fP
for copy or nvlist-unpacking failures, or \fBNDI_FAILURE\fP for an invalid
nvlist buffer size.
The output is valid only on success.
The accessors return borrowed pointers or \fBNULL\fP.
\fBndi_dc_freehdl()\fP has no return value.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ndi_dc_devi_create 9F ,
.Xr ndi_dc_return_dev_state 9F ,
.Xr ndi_devctl_ioctl 9F ,
.Xr sunndi 9F
.Sh NOTES
\fBndi_dc_getpath()\fP and \fBndi_dc_getminorname()\fP are declared in
\fBsys/sunndi.h\fP but have no implementation in illumos.
Do not use them.
